 "_doc": [
  "Idiomatic lead-ins for the commonest section headings, by ISO 639-3.",
  "A field listed here is introduced as a speaker would introduce it -- 'In",
  "der Szene:' rather than 'Szene:'; anything else keeps the translated",
  "noun, which is what the heading machinery already produces.",
  "",
  "Partial on purpose, and partial in the same way English is: the English",
  "pack writes fifty of the two hundred and forty-seven field names the",
  "lessons use, and the rest appear as bare headings. Mixing the two is the",
  "existing design rather than a compromise introduced here.",
  "",
  "Fourteen fields, which is a third of all block occurrences. Only",
  "languages whose wording could be checked; the rest fall back, visibly.",
  "",
  "Russian and Polish are written as labels rather than clauses because",
  "that is how those languages head a section -- 'Правила:' and not a",
  "copular sentence, which would read as translated English.",
  "",
  "survive, and the rest of the French output -- headings, questions -- is",
  "",
  "French is written with a plain colon here and the space is added by the",
  "typography, which knows which marks the language sets off -- so the intros",
  "match its headings and its questions instead of being the only spaced line."
